  "_comments": {
    "experiment_a": "Six-cell architecture-by-compression sweep. Every run uses continuous truncation, max_seq_len=256, latent_dim=32, K=3072, K-means initialization, EMA decay 0.99, double L2 normalization, and no AE warmup. Compression ratios 2/4/8 use latent_slots 128/64/32. Each ratio compares RoPE+memory_trunk with VQGANR+VQGANR; VQGANR uses 5/2/1 ResBlocks to keep parameter counts approximately matched.",
    "experiment_a_parameter_counts": "Current counts are ratio-2: 24.81M RoPE vs 23.42M VQGANR; ratio-4: 25.21M vs 25.03M; ratio-8: 26.01M vs 26.64M.",
    "experiment_b": "Three-cell EMA-decay sweep. Every run fixes K=8192, latent_dim=32, RoPE+memory_trunk, compression ratio 2, K-means initialization, adaptive AE warmup, no continuous truncation, and no L2 normalization. Only ema_decay changes: 0.99, 0.95, or 0.9.",
    "experiment_b_adaptive_warmup": "Adaptive warmup uses min_steps=1000, max_steps=6000, check_every=200, patience=5, dimension_tolerance=1, probe_points=8192, and variance_threshold=0.99.",
    "sample_limits": "max_train_samples and max_eval_samples are not overridden; both experiments use the DataConfig defaults. In experiment A, max_train_samples limits source texts before continuous truncation expands them into chunks."
